# U-Boot's extlinux/syslinux parser and fw_setenv do NOT tolerate CRLF: a
# trailing \r ends up glued to the DTB path / kernel cmdline / env value and
# the board fails to boot (hangs right after the splash). These were committed
# with CRLF once and cost a long debugging session - force LF forever.
**/boot/extlinux/extlinux.conf text eol=lf
**/boot/*.env text eol=lf
# Target shell scripts and init scripts must be LF too (a \r in the shebang or
# a line makes /bin/sh choke).
**/overlay/**/*.sh text eol=lf
**/overlay/**/etc/init.d/* text eol=lf
